  "term": "temporal lobe epilepsy",
  "definition": "Temporal lobe epilepsy is a common form of epilepsy in which seizures begin in mesial temporal brain structures. In the cognition context, it is linked with broader brain network abnormalities beyond the temporal lobes that can affect cognitive performance, including working memory and other memory functions.",
